# The image is published; the working tree is not. This file decides what a
# published container carries.
#
# It is an allow-list on purpose. As a deny-list it shipped whatever nobody
# remembered to add: .gitignore already kept docs/example_UC/ (NDA-covered) and
# CHANGELOG_data_model.md out of the repository, but the build copied them into
# the image regardless, because .dockerignore and .gitignore are unrelated
# files. Excluding everything and naming what the app reads means a new private
# folder is left out by default rather than by vigilance.
*

# What the running app reads
!python/src
!ontology
!shacl
!external

# Attribution and licence travel with the code
!NOTICE.md
!LICENSE
!README.md

# ...and what must never ship, even from inside those trees. The user's own
# architecture graphs - confidential, NDA-covered, unfinished - are gitignored
# too, so usually absent from a checkout; excluded here as well because a build
# can run from a dirty tree.
ontology/example_local
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
